      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"how-does-search-work\">How Does Search Work?</h3></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "GQNb",
      "code_hash": "e71cac6f3254b0010d49b9d496761bee",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>InMemoryService (this notebook):</strong></span>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Method:</strong> Keyword matching</span>\n<ul>\n<li><em>e.g.</em> \"favorite color\" matches\nbecause those exact words exist</li>\n<li><strong>Limitation:</strong> age won't match even\nthough it's relevant to the memory</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>VertexAiMemoryBankService/Production</strong>:</span>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Method:</strong> Semantic search via <em>embeddings</em></span>\n<ul>\n<li><em>e.g.</em> \"age\" will likely match birthday \nconversations</li>\n<li><strong>Advantage:</strong> Understands meaning, not\njust keywords</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ZyQD",
      "code_hash": "339a6eba06a9ba62b3fcb461557fda86",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"automating-memory-storage\">Automating Memory Storage</h3></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nBqv",
      "code_hash": "38c60c5e0b60c62af98429b5c36ed067",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Callbacks</strong>\nADK has a callback system that hooks into\nkey execution moments.</span>\n<ul>\n<li>callbacks are <strong>python functions</strong> that are\nattached to agents.</li>\n<li>ADK automatically calls them at specific\nstages - sort of like checkpoints during\nthe execution flow.</li>\n<li><strong>Think of callbacks as event listeners in\nthe agent lifecyle</strong></li>\n<li>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">e.g. When agent processes a request...</span>\n<ul>\n<li>Agent receives input</li>\n<li>Agent calls the LLM</li>\n<li>Agent invokes tools</li>\n<li>Agent generates the response</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Callbacks let users insert custom logic at\neach of the stages above <em>without</em> modifying\ncore agent code.</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "liRI",
      "code_hash": "40780128dcc69c10e37fee3f2e35041c",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Available callback types and usecases:</strong></span>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Runs before OR after agent completes\nprocessing a request</span>\n<ul>\n<li><code>before_agent_callback</code></li>\n<li><code>after_agent_callback</code></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Around tool invocations</span>\n<ul>\n<li><code>before_tool_callback</code></li>\n<li><code>after_tool_callback</code></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Around LLM calls</span>\n<ul>\n<li><code>before_model_callback</code></li>\n<li><code>after_model_callback</code></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>When errors occur: <code>on_model_error_callback</code></li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "lpuM",
      "code_hash": "ec3b991ca5bbd98854c38028766bf9eb",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Common Uses:</strong></span>\n<ul>\n<li>Logging and observabnility of agent actions</li>\n<li>Automatic data persistence</li>\n<li>Custom validation/filtering</li>\n<li>Performance monitoring</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"https://google.github.io/adk-docs/agents/callbacks/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">ADK Callbacks Doco</a></span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "tDaU",
      "code_hash": "b7beb57cbe7232230573058aac2c179f",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Automatic Memory Storage with Callbacks</strong></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">For automatic memory storage we'll\n use <code>after_agent_callback</code>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">After every agent turn this calls\n <code>add_session_to_memory()</code>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This is able to access the memory service through\n <code>callback_context</code>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">When a callback function is defined, ADK passes\n a special paramter call <code>callback_context</code> to it.\n The <code>callback_context</code> provides access to the\n Memory Service and other runtine components.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">In our callback we'll have access the\nmemory service and current session to \nauto-save the convo data every turn.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "DWct",
      "code_hash": "e28f6449f45c33126e7220a1d484427c",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<marimo-callout-output data-html='&quot;&lt;span class=&#92;&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents&#92;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&gt;You do no create the context - ADK does&#92;nit for us and passes it to our callback&#92;nautomatically when the callback runs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&quot;' data-kind='&quot;info&quot;'></marimo-callout-output>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Rdec",
      "code_hash": "27a8ca86f7372e683893d1c3e0363584",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": ""
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": [
        {
          "type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": "Callback created! :)\n",
          "mimetype": "text/plain"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "IkwK",
      "code_hash": "fb25642ba30d944f984e6ff6779d3b94",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Create an Agent: Callback and Preload Memory Tool</strong></span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "KyWM",
      "code_hash": "315609ad9d752faf66ef9e8725515b36",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Now we're going to create an agent thay combines:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Automatic storage:</strong> <code>after_agent_callback</code>\nsaves conversations</li>\n<li><strong>Automatic retrieval:</strong> <code>preload_memory</code> loads\nmemories.</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Together this creates a fully automated memory \nsystem with no manual intervention.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
